# Test Files Organization

## Test Directory Structure

**ALL test files must be placed in the `tests/` directory** to maintain a clean project structure and proper organization.

### ✅ Correct Test File Locations

```
tests/
├── test_single_bjs.sh           # Single file BJS testing
├── test_single_upgrade.sh       # Single file upgrade testing
├── test_version3_loading.sh     # Version 3 loading tests
├── test_upgrade_process.sh      # Upgrade process tests
├── test_generated_code.sh       # Generated code validation
├── sample_working_gladeui.vala  # Sample test files
└── README.md                    # Test documentation
```

### ❌ Incorrect Test File Locations

```
# DON'T put test files in project root
test_single_bjs.sh              # Wrong location
test_upgrade_process.sh         # Wrong location

# DON'T put test files in src/
src/test_*.sh                   # Wrong location
src/tests/                      # Wrong location
```

## Test File Naming Conventions

### Bash Test Scripts

```bash
# Pattern: test_<functionality>.sh
test_single_bjs.sh              # Test single BJS file
test_single_upgrade.sh          # Test single upgrade
test_version3_loading.sh        # Test version 3 loading
test_upgrade_process.sh         # Test upgrade process
test_generated_code.sh          # Test code generation
test_compilation.sh             # Test compilation
test_symbol_loading.sh          # Test symbol loading
```

### Vala Test Files

```vala
// Pattern: test_<component>.vala or sample_<description>.vala
test_node.vala                  // Test Node class
test_nodeprop.vala              // Test NodeProp class
sample_working_gladeui.vala     // Sample working file
test_serialization.vala         // Test serialization
```

### Python Test Files

```python
# Pattern: test_<module>.py
test_brace_formatting.py        # Test brace formatting
test_indentation.py             # Test indentation
test_file_processing.py         # Test file processing
```

## Test Script Requirements

### Shebang and Debug Mode

```bash
#!/bin/bash -x

# Always use -x for debugging visibility
# This shows command execution and variable expansion
```

### Path Handling from tests/ Directory

```bash
# Correct path references from tests/ directory
if [[ ! -f "../build/roobuilder" ]]; then
    echo "ERROR: Local build not found at ../build/roobuilder"
    exit 1
fi

# Use relative paths for project files
../build/roobuilder --project /home/alan/gitlive/roobuilder --test-bjs-upgrade "$file"

# Reference source files with relative paths
BJS_FILE="../src/Builder4/About.bjs"
```

### Test Directory Structure

```bash
# Create test results in /tmp with timestamp
TEST_DIR="/tmp/test_$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S)"
mkdir -p "$TEST_DIR"

# Separate output files
OUTPUT_FILE="$TEST_DIR/${filename}_output.log"
ERROR_FILE="$TEST_DIR/${filename}_error.log"
RESULTS_LOG="$TEST_DIR/test_results.log"
```

